    "content": {
     "header": "Sommer am Ursprung",
     "subheader": "",
     "headerLayout": 0,
     "headerPosition": "",
     "headerLink": "",
     "type": "mask_imgtext",
     "title": "",
     "text": "<p>Up here, time loses its meaning. Dew on the meadows, cool shade in the woods, light that lingers. The day begins without urgency: a window left open, earthy herbs in the air, wide horizons ahead. Steps turn into thoughts. Pauses arrive on their own. Mountain summer asks for nothing and gives so much in return.<br>Days grow long, the light turns soft, and nature sets the pace. Summer warmth rests over the alpine pastures; the hum of bees in clover accompanies every step.<br>And suddenly, it’s there: a simplicity that carries.</p>",
